    "A brass lever joins a switch flask to a gate. While the gate's bars are down, nothing pours into it or out of it." : {

    },
    "A crossing carries two pipes over each other. They never mix, so two potions can pass through the same spot." : {
      "comment" : "Distillery tip: cross pieces"
    },
    "A flask etched with a glowing rune takes only the potion of that rune. Anything else is refused, even when the flask is empty." : {

    },
    "A flask that stirs itself? I like this bog." : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 7 (Bubbling Bog)"
    },
    "A flask with a brass funnel takes potions in like any flask, but nothing ever pours out of it." : {

    },
    "A flask with a brass tap pours from the bottom: the bottom potion runs out of the tap and the rest slides down." : {

    },
    "A flask with a narrow neck and a brass collar lets one layer through per pour, even when more would fit." : {

    },
    "A frozen ingredient can't be swapped. Match it, or match right beside it, to crack one layer of ice. Thick frost needs two." : {
      "comment" : "Match-3 tip: frost tiles"
    },
    "A funnel flask only fills. Nothing pours out of it." : {
      "comment" : "Shown when the player tries to pour from a funnel flask"
    },
    "A glowing coil brews the potion passing through it: the tag in its corner shows what goes in and what comes out. Other potions pass unchanged." : {
      "comment" : "Distillery tip: heat coils change a color"
    },
    "A hint was used, so no gold seal this time" : {

    },
    "A hint was used, so this brew can't be perfect" : {

    },
    "A hint was used, so two stars at most" : {

    },
    "A narrow neck lets one layer through at a time, a funnel only takes potions in, and a tap pours from the bottom. Each one changes how the potions flow." : {
      "comment" : "Story, chapter 5 (Glass Works)"
    },
    "A new recipe to crack, as many times as you like. Nothing is saved." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint: Secret Recipe practice"
